<ArticleLayout title="Original Homeowner Research: Methods Before Results" description="Planned generator quote, reliability, warranty and ownership studies with transparent sampling, privacy and publication requirements." category="Research" categoryHref="/guides/" published="2026-10-07" updated="2026-10-07" readingTime="6 min read" toc={[]} sources={[]}>
<p><strong>Quick answer:</strong> Data collection is pending. We have no published study participants, verified quote results or original failure-rate estimates. This framework defines what must exist before results are released.</p>
<h2>What can be used today?</h2>
<p>The <a href="/planning/quotes/">browser-local three-quote planner</a> helps individual homeowners compare scope without transmitting documents. A <a href="/templates/standby-quote-pilot-blank.csv" download>blank, non-identifying pilot worksheet</a> is also available for private use. Neither generates a research submission or provides evidence of a national price distribution.</p>
<h2>Planned research questions</h2><ul>{STUDY_TOPICS.map(title=><li><strong>{title}</strong> — protocol planning; no results published.</li>)}</ul>
<h2>The protocol each study must publish</h2><ol><li>Research question, version and dates; eligibility, recruitment channels, inclusion and exclusion rules.</li><li>Questionnaire, definitions, observation period and denominators. A year-three study needs ownership duration and exposure, not just complaints.</li><li>Consent, private storage, redaction, retention, withdrawal and deletion process before collection starts.</li><li>Household/project deduplication, linked follow-ups and quote-versus-invoice separation.</li><li>Missing responses, sponsorship or compensation, sampling biases and limits on generalization.</li><li>Analysis plan, sample-size rationale, publication threshold and independent editorial review.</li></ol>
<h2>Publication gates</h2><p>For quote cohorts, fewer than 20 independent verified projects means no distribution is published. This editorial floor does not make larger samples representative. Reliability claims need a separate precision and sampling plan; the quote threshold cannot be reused as proof of a failure rate. No significance claims or national averages will be inferred from self-selected participants.</p>
<h2>Future table and chart requirements</h2><p>Every result must include the question, unit, sample size, denominator, period, geography, configuration mix, missing-data count, inclusion rules and uncertainty. Quote charts will separate proposals from invoices and show median, quartiles and observed range. No placeholder bars or synthetic participants appear as findings.</p>
<h2>Privacy and corrections</h2><p>No survey or upload is open. Research participation will be separate from browser-local tools. Participants will need a documented withdrawal route and retention terms before submitting. Public exports must exclude original documents and private identifiers; small geographic groups require suppression.</p><p>See the <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a>, <a href="/corrections-policy/">corrections policy</a>, <a href="/cost/homeowner-quote-database/">verified quote project</a>, <a href="/research/evidence-ledger/">weakness evidence method</a> and <a href="/research/local-service/">serviceability study method</a>.</p>
</ArticleLayout>
